      "writtenOn": "2018-08-10T10:36:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this true today? I don\u0027t think so - and I don\u0027t think it should be. I think an unscoped token should only ever be used to be exchanged for a scoped token. We should create something else, like a user scope or a my-own-project scope to describe things like this.\n\nIs there any use case where operators would want to use policy to restrict a user\u0027s ability to create SSH keypairs for themselves? I don\u0027t think we have any mechanism today to create rules for unscoped tokens.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "70e60535f8b88a408b9875d7e112a77e1ac5ac34",
